WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.548
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online Advanced.

2
00:00:05.848 --> 00:00:09.060
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:17.179
Unit twenty-four: The Future of Cities in Asia. In this unit, you will discuss rapid urban growth in Asia.

4
00:00:18.183 --> 00:00:19.835
rapid urbanisation.

5
00:00:20.535 --> 00:00:25.750
rapid urbanisation means the fast growth of cities as people move from rural areas.

6
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:30.023
Rapid urbanisation is transforming Southeast Asia.

7
00:00:30.723 --> 00:00:34.235
Your turn. Say: rapid urbanisation.

8
00:00:36.935 --> 00:00:38.621
rapid urbanisation.

9
00:00:39.617 --> 00:00:41.094
informal settlement.

10
00:00:41.794 --> 00:00:46.580
informal settlement means an area of homes built without official permission.

11
00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:50.447
Many workers live in informal settlements near factories.

12
00:00:51.147 --> 00:00:54.252
Your turn. Say: informal settlement.

13
00:00:56.952 --> 00:00:58.336
informal settlement.

14
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:00.850
satellite city.

15
00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:05.303
satellite city means a new town built near a larger city.

16
00:01:05.603 --> 00:01:09.042
Several satellite cities are planned around Phnom Penh.

17
00:01:09.742 --> 00:01:13.091
Your turn. Say: satellite city.

18
00:01:15.791 --> 00:01:17.013
satellite city.

19
00:01:18.017 --> 00:01:19.877
special economic zone.

20
00:01:20.577 --> 00:01:26.617
special economic zone means an area with special business and tax rules to attract investment.

21
00:01:26.917 --> 00:01:30.832
The special economic zone in Sihanoukville attracted foreign factories.

22
00:01:31.532 --> 00:01:35.345
Your turn. Say: special economic zone.

23
00:01:38.045 --> 00:01:39.987
special economic zone.

24
00:01:40.983 --> 00:01:42.251
flood management.

25
00:01:42.951 --> 00:01:46.275
flood management means measures to reduce damage from floods.

26
00:01:46.575 --> 00:01:50.629
Better flood management is vital for low-lying cities.

27
00:01:51.329 --> 00:01:54.655
Your turn. Say: flood management.

28
00:01:57.355 --> 00:01:58.542
flood management.

29
00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.015
smart transport.

30
00:02:01.715 --> 00:02:06.873
smart transport means transport systems that use data and technology.

31
00:02:07.173 --> 00:02:09.974
Smart transport can reduce traffic jams.

32
00:02:10.674 --> 00:02:14.220
Your turn. Say: smart transport.

33
00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:18.409
smart transport.

34
00:02:19.417 --> 00:02:20.812
urban migration.

35
00:02:21.512 --> 00:02:25.509
urban migration means people moving from the countryside to cities.

36
00:02:25.809 --> 00:02:28.842
Urban migration has doubled the capital's population.

37
00:02:29.542 --> 00:02:33.065
Your turn. Say: urban migration.

38
00:02:35.765 --> 00:02:37.068
urban migration.

39
00:02:38.083 --> 00:02:39.560
land speculation.

40
00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:44.907
land speculation means buying land to sell later at a higher price.

41
00:02:45.207 --> 00:02:48.112
Land speculation has pushed up housing costs.

42
00:02:48.812 --> 00:02:52.358
Your turn. Say: land speculation.

43
00:02:55.058 --> 00:02:56.501
land speculation.

44
00:02:57.517 --> 00:02:59.690
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:03.139
Rithy, what struck you most when you moved to Phnom Penh?

46
00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:07.715
What struck me most was how fast everything was changing.

47
00:03:09.017 --> 00:03:13.318
Rapid urbanisation, yes. It's the same across much of Asia.

48
00:03:14.617 --> 00:03:19.475
It's land speculation that worries me. Ordinary families can't afford homes.

49
00:03:20.783 --> 00:03:24.629
And many end up in informal settlements without proper services.

50
00:03:25.917 --> 00:03:27.847
Are satellite cities the answer?

51
00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:35.436
Only if they're well connected. What these cities need is smart transport and serious flood management.

52
00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:40.259
All we need, really, is planning that puts people first.

53
00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:45.337
Grammar focus: Cleft sentences in discussion.

54
00:03:45.637 --> 00:03:49.193
Cleft sentences help you highlight your main point in a discussion.

55
00:03:49.493 --> 00:03:55.024
What struck me most was the speed of change. It's land speculation that worries me.

56
00:03:55.324 --> 00:03:57.289
All we need is better planning.

57
00:03:57.589 --> 00:04:02.596
In discussions, cleft sentences help you highlight your main concern clearly.

58
00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:07.002
Now read and listen. Asia's Urban Century.

59
00:04:07.302 --> 00:04:13.911
By 2050, Asia's cities are expected to house an additional one billion people.

60
00:04:15.217 --> 00:04:20.676
Urban migration brings workers to factories, offices and special economic zones.

61
00:04:21.983 --> 00:04:26.421
What often follows, however, is a severe shortage of affordable housing.

62
00:04:27.717 --> 00:04:33.907
Land speculation drives up prices, pushing low-income families into informal settlements.

63
00:04:35.217 --> 00:04:43.207
Many Asian cities are also low-lying, making flood management an urgent priority.

64
00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:49.175
Governments are planning satellite cities to reduce pressure on overcrowded centres.

65
00:04:50.483 --> 00:04:56.198
It is good transport connections, though, that determine whether these new towns succeed.

66
00:04:57.483 --> 00:05:02.118
The future of Asia's cities will shape the lives of billions of people.

67
00:05:03.417 --> 00:05:06.150
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

68
00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:10.435
An area of homes built without official permission is an blank.

69
00:05:10.735 --> 00:05:16.850
A, informal settlement. B, satellite city. C, special economic zone.

70
00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:23.604
The answer is A: informal settlement.

71
00:05:25.117 --> 00:05:27.534
blank surprised me was the traffic.

72
00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:30.907
A, It. B, What. C, That.

73
00:05:34.917 --> 00:05:36.626
The answer is B: What.

74
00:05:38.117 --> 00:05:40.534
It was the noise blank annoyed me most.

75
00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:44.325
A, what. B, that. C, which it.

76
00:05:48.317 --> 00:05:50.723
The answer is B: that.

77
00:05:52.217 --> 00:05:55.784
Buying land to sell later at a higher price is blank.

78
00:05:56.084 --> 00:06:02.024
A, land speculation. B, urban migration. C, flood management.

79
00:06:06.017 --> 00:06:08.817
The answer is A: land speculation.

80
00:06:10.317 --> 00:06:14.778
According to the text, what determines whether satellite cities succeed?

81
00:06:15.078 --> 00:06:20.716
A, good transport connections. B, shopping malls. C, tall buildings.

82
00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:28.272
The answer is A: good transport connections.

83
00:06:29.783 --> 00:06:35.129
Now it's your turn. Part one: What is the biggest challenge facing Asian cities?

84
00:06:40.429 --> 00:06:45.447
Part two: Use a cleft sentence, explain two causes, and propose one solution.

85
00:06:51.747 --> 00:07:04.027
What concerns me most is housing affordability. It's caused by land speculation and rapid migration. All we really need is a large public housing programme connected to good transport.

86
00:07:04.327 --> 00:07:06.640
That is a well-argued answer!

87
00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:12.508
Great work today! You learned eight new words and cleft sentences in discussion.

88
00:07:12.808 --> 00:07:16.691
Today's value is community. Help the people in your town.

89
00:07:16.991 --> 00:07:21.373
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

90
00:07:21.673 --> 00:07:24.686
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

